From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP player-loader load loop matches skipped cuts

skipCutHole can dequeue hole keys so the ticket list is shorter than
maxLoadsThisTick. The follow-up scheduleChunkLoad loop still indexed the
original count and IOBE'd the region tick. Iterate the list that was
actually queued. Carve stays on. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java
@@ -722,7 +722,7 @@
             final int maxLoadsThisTick = (int)this.chunkLoadTicketLimiter.takeAllocation(maxLoads);
             if (maxLoadsThisTick > 0) {
                 final LongArrayList chunks = new LongArrayList(maxLoadsThisTick);
-                for (int i = 0; i < maxLoadsThisTick && !this.loadQueue.isEmpty(); ++i) {
+                while (chunks.size() < maxLoadsThisTick && !this.loadQueue.isEmpty()) {
                     final long chunk = this.loadQueue.firstLong();
                     final int loadX = CoordinateUtils.getChunkX(chunk);
                     final int loadZ = CoordinateUtils.getChunkZ(chunk);
@@ -757,7 +757,7 @@
                     return;
                 }
 
-                for (int i = 0; i < maxLoadsThisTick; ++i) {
+                for (int i = 0, n = chunks.size(); i < n; ++i) {
                     final long queuedLoadChunk = chunks.getLong(i);
                     final int queuedChunkX = CoordinateUtils.getChunkX(queuedLoadChunk);
                     final int queuedChunkZ = CoordinateUtils.getChunkZ(queuedLoadChunk);
